  "description": "Haydock's annotated Douay-Rheims, first issued in parts from 1811 and reprinted through the nineteenth century. The commentary is a compilation of Catholic exegetes with initialled attributions: C. for Calmet, H. for Haydock, M. for Menochius, W. for Worthington, and others, expanded in the edition's own key. The scriptural text it prints is Challoner's revision; the notes are the work registered here. A locus is BookToken.chapter.verse.",
